Marker file to nudge a GitHub Pages redeploy.

GitHub's built-in "pages build and deployment" occasionally fails on a
transient GitHub-side issue — either an OIDC 503 ("Failed to get ID
Token / reset reason: overflow") or the deployment sitting in
"deployment_queued" until the action times out and aborts. Both are
GitHub infra hiccups, not a repo config problem. When it happens the
live dashboard lags one deploy behind while the data in the repo is
already correct. Touching this file re-triggers the Pages deploy without
running the counting workflow (docs/ is not in its path filter).

Last nudges:
- 2026-07-09: deploy failed on OIDC 503 (run 29019449249).
- 2026-08-06: deploy timed out in deployment_queued (run 31101345885).
